# nagios-checks.conf - Nagios checks on agents (nagios-checks.sh)
#
# Copy to nagios-checks.conf next to nagios-checks.sh. One key per line.
# Comments go on their own line only: a '#' after a value becomes part of the
# value.
#
#   schedule = <cron expression>                  when run-jobs runs the job
#   check    = <agent> <check-name> [<check-name> ...]
#                                                 the checks to run on that agent
#
# Check names are the keys in the agent's checks.conf; list them, and
# see whether each plugin is installed there (available true or false), with
#   ctrl-exec-cli run <agent> --script nagios-check -- --list
# Only names go over the wire. Thresholds, plugin and arguments are the
# agent's own.
#
# Each check line is one call to the agent, and the checks in one call run one
# after another within the agent's run budget (default 50 s, below the
# dispatcher's read_timeout of 60 s). An agent may have several check lines:
# each is a separate call. Split local checks (disk, load, mem: quick) from
# network checks (http, ping, dns: can wait for their timeout) so that a slow
# network check cannot use up the time of the local ones.

schedule = */5 * * * *

check = agent-01 disk_root load swap
check = agent-02 disk_root load
check = agent-03 http_example

# Two lines for one agent: local checks, then network checks
check = agent-04 disk load mem
check = agent-04 web_health ping_gateway
